{"id":"n5-047","title":"Verb て います","romaji":"Verb te imasu","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Express ongoing action or state; 'is doing', 'is doing (continuous)', 'has been doing'.","longExplanation":"The て います grammar point is used to express an action that is ongoing, continuous, or has been happening. It is formed by conjugating the verb in its て-form and adding います. It can be translated as 'is doing', 'is doing (continuous)', or 'has been doing' in English.","formation":"Verb て-form + います","examples":[{"jp":"彼女は今ピアノを弾いています。","romaji":"Kanojo wa ima piano wo hiite imasu.","en":"She is playing the piano now.","words":[{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"今","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ピアノ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"弾い","vocabId":"1419370","reading":"ひく","baseForm":"弾く"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[7,8]},{"jp":"私たちは日本語を勉強しています。","romaji":"Watashitachi wa nihongo wo benkyou shiteimasu.","en":"We are studying Japanese.","words":[{"surface":"私たち","vocabId":"1311300","reading":"わたしたち"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"日本語","vocabId":"1464530","reading":"にほんご"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"勉強","vocabId":"1512670","reading":"べんきょう"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[7,8]},{"jp":"彼は映画を見ています。","romaji":"Kare wa eiga wo miteimasu.","en":"He is watching a movie.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"映画","vocabId":"1173720","reading":"えいが"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"見","vocabId":"1259290","reading":"みる","baseForm":"見る"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","voca